# IP Management UX

IP Management owns **inpatient / day-care operational workflow**: census, admission, bed assignment/transfer, ward assignment, `PatientJourney`, IP status, pre-op readiness, discharge/transfer operations, IP dashboards.

Canonical UI: `src/components/ip-management/` + `src/lib/ip-management/` + `/dashboard/ip-management/*`, wrapped in `IpTargetFrame` / `.ip-target`. Canonical overlay: `IpOverlayDialog`. Do not add `fixed inset-0` overlays; `ip-overlays-consolidated.test.ts` enforces this.

Also follow `.cursor/rules/ip-billing-ward-cross-module.mdc`.

## Canonical routes (do not invent parallel IP apps)

| Workflow | Route |
|---|---|
| Census | `/dashboard/ip-management` |
| Ward | `/dashboard/ip-management/ward` |
| OT board | `/dashboard/ip-management/operation-theatre` |
| Slots / throughput | `/dashboard/ip-management/slots`, `/throughput` |
| IP billing worklist | `/dashboard/ip-management/billing` (lens + deep link to OpdBill — not a second ledger) |
| Journey | `/dashboard/ip-management/journey/[id]` |

Do not revive `/dashboard/operations/ot` mocks as the production OT/IP board. Do not merge IP into a new `/ward` or `/clinical` tree without approval.

## Must not duplicate

- Billing ownership (charges, payments, refunds, receipts) — Billing `OpdBill`
- Coverage/claims ownership — CCMS
- OT financial logic
- Bed occupancy SoT — Auth bed inventory
- Frontend-owned financial totals (`FinancialState`, `TotalPaid`, `IpBillingTransaction` are projections; use `IpFinancialFieldClassification`; never silently overwrite)

## UX expectations

High-frequency operational board: keyboard where census already supports it, patient identification always visible, readiness/gates explicit, stale/realtime connection visible. Prefer existing primitives (`StatusChip`, bed map, rails, workspace modals) over new chrome.

UAT seeder `/dashboard/dev/uat` is development-only — do not wire it into production journeys.
